    $K[M]$ is the union of the ideals $I_M (M_s)$, $s = 1, ..., q$. Since $I_f$
    contains at least one nondivisor of zero, then $I_f inter I_M (M_s)$ is a
    proper subspace of $I_f$ for any $s$. If all the nondivisors of zero
    contained in $I_f$ had belonged to some of its proper subspaces, then $I_f$
    would have been a union of a finite number of proper subspaces which is
    impossible.]

  #hint[@pr:everywhere-defined-is-polynomial][Let $f$ be such a function. The
    conditions of the problem imply that the variety of zeros of $I_f$ is empty.
    By Problem~@pr:weak-nullstellensatz-on-variety this implies that
    $I_f in.rev 1$, i.e. $f$ is presentable in the form $f = g\/1$, where
    $g in K[M]$, as required.]

  #hint[@pr:rational-functions-on-principal-open][Is solved like
    Problem~@pr:everywhere-defined-is-polynomial but with the help of Hilbert’s
    Nullstellensatz itself.]

  #hint[@pr:definedness-from-restriction][Passing to an appropriate dense
    principal open subset reduce to the case when $M' inter M'' = emptyset$ and
    use Problem~@pr:disjoint-union-coordinate-algebra.]

  #hint[@pr:rational-functions-product-components][Passing to an appropriate
    dense principal open subset reduce to the case when irreducible components
    of $M$ do not intersect and use
    Problem~@pr:disjoint-union-coordinate-algebra.]

